From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:17:27 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/79] core: sandboxed compute lane executor (Landlock +
 seccomp)

The executor the compute lane runs a model's Python call in. Nothing uses it
yet; the lane itself follows separately.

- compute_lane.zig: Config (workers, wall/memory/output limits, result and
  call caps, interpreter path, CPU list) parsed from PREFIX and PREFIX_*
  knobs, where only "1" enables; a pool of sandbox slots and the supervisor
  of one job: posix_spawn of the trampoline, pidfd, wall limit, output cap,
  cancel.
- compute_sandbox.zig: the trampoline a fresh process runs before exec'ing
  Python: drops root to nobody, sets rlimits and CPU affinity, keeps an
  inherited niceness at or above 10 (a dropped uid may not lower it), then
  applies Landlock and seccomp.
- compute_landlock.zig: read and execute beneath the interpreter's roots
  only; no writes, no network, no signals out.
- compute_seccomp.zig: native arch only; no sockets, tracing, namespaces or
  child processes.
- compute_runner.zig: the Python prelude (stdin source, REPL-style repr of a
  final bare expression, seeded random) and the canonical, deterministic
  result text of one job.

Linux only: elsewhere a job is "unavailable". test-compute-lane-host runs
jobs through the real sandbox: confinement, limits, output cap, cancel,
niceness and result text.
